","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-06-14T13:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T18:09:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7 rc2 (Android)\n- not reproducible in 4.6.3 (stable) (android)\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid 14\n\n### Issue description\n\n- when auto recompiling shaders after making a change there is a chance that the editor will freeze momentarily and in projects with a significant amount going on (not sure if it's shaders currently being used or just how much stuff is currently loaded in general that makes the difference) it happens more often and past a certain amount results in a crash.\n- changing a shader shouldn't cause a freeze or crash\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create or open a project\n- Create or open a shader (it happens more often if the shader is attached to an object in the current scene but has happened when this isn't the case)\n- make changes waiting in between so it can attempt to recompile (commenting and uncommenting a line or pasting / removing a line is enough)\n- after a few changes it will freeze momentarily or crash\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shader crash MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28928462/shader.crash.MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120288/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"hear